  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Team Garage Desk",
    "overview": "A working tool that could only belong to Longhorn Racing. The system is the LHR Brand Book's \"structured approachability\" carried into product UI: white rectangles with soft rounded corners set on the brand's Light Gray, Ocean Blue as the one voice for action and selection, and Montserrat titles over Urbanist reading text. Expression does not come from ornament. It comes from three real things: the official logos, the team-colour stripes, and photographs of the cars from the team galleries.\n\nDensity is that of a quiet tool. Pages open on a noun title and a single line of context, then go straight to panels, forms and tables. Tables are built from hairline rules and alignment, never zebra bands. Every surface sits flat; depth is drawn with 1px rules and tonal steps between Light Gray, white and a near-white mist.\n\nThe one expressive surface is sign-in: a full-height team photograph (one of the three teams, rotating daily) beside a white panel holding the CAREERS lockup, a \"Sign in\" headline, one sentence, a two-door switch (LHR member / Partner) and Google sign-in as the primary action.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Ocean Blue on Light Gray with white surfaces; ink-blue text, never pure black.",
      "Soft rounded rectangles: 8px for controls, 16px for panels, 6px for small chips.",
      "Flat surfaces separated by 1px rules; no card shadows.",
      "Montserrat 600 for titles, buttons and choice labels; Urbanist for everything read.",
      "Team ambers appear only as team coding: stripes, logos, photographs.",
      "Official logo artwork only, full colour on light, white on dark."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Voice Rule",
        "body": "Ocean Blue is the only colour that means \"act here\" or \"you are here\". Nothing else is filled blue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Team Coding Rule",
        "body": "Solar, Electric and Combustion ambers mark a team and nothing else: never a button, a warning, a highlight or a decorative accent.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mid Gray Rule",
        "body": "Mid Gray never carries text. It fails contrast; secondary text is Slate.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The No Burnt Orange Rule",
        "body": "UT Burnt Orange (#BF5700) and colours near it are trademarked and never appear. The team ambers sit well to the yellow side of it; keep it that way.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Title Case Voice Rule",
        "body": "Montserrat is set at 600 in sentence case. Uppercase Montserrat is reserved for the CAREERS descriptor inside the lockup artwork, which is never re-typeset in live text.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Eurostile Rule",
        "body": "Eurostile Extended exists only inside the logo files. It is never loaded as a web font.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Surface Rule",
        "body": "Resting surfaces never cast shadows. A shadow means \"this floats above the page\" and is reserved for overlays.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use only the official LHR logo files in `public/brand/`: full colour on light grounds, the white version on dark. Follow the brand book's order: logoblock, then primary or team logo, then the three-stripe shortmark (favicon), then the wordmark.",
      "**Do** pair any descriptor such as \"CAREERS\" with the logo, set in Montserrat caps per the brand book's logo-descriptor rule.",
      "**Do** open every app page with a noun title at Headline size (about 28px) and one line of context.",
      "**Do** mark teams with their own amber (Solar #FF9404, Electric #FFB526, Combustion #FFC871) and their official team logo, and nowhere else.",
      "**Do** use real team photographs from the longhornracing.org Solar, Electric and Combustion galleries for imagery.",
      "**Do** keep every control at least 40px tall with the 2px Ocean Blue focus outline.",
      "**Do** build tables from 1px rules and alignment."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** recolour, crop, fade, outline or re-typeset any logo, and never use a black logo.",
      "**Don't** use UT Burnt Orange #BF5700 or any colour near it.",
      "**Don't** write \"sponsor\" anywhere: copy, URLs, alt text or code. Companies are \"Partners\".",
      "**Don't** use \"IC\" or \"EV\" in public copy, or \"UT Austin's LHR\". Teams are Solar, Electric and Combustion (LHRs, LHRe, LHRc); the name is \"Longhorn Racing\" or \"LHR\".",
      "**Don't** set text in Mid Gray #9CADB7; it fails contrast.",
      "**Don't** put shadows on resting panels, tiles or bars.",
      "**Don't** use team ambers for buttons, warnings, badges or decoration.",
      "**Don't** add a sidebar to the app shell.",
      "**Don't** load Eurostile Extended as a web font.",
      "**Don't** put eyebrow or kicker labels above titles."
    ]
  }
}
